This design pattern is usefully when we have a large system with many classes that are independent of one another
In many cases, clients only need a small part of such APIs
Facade provides a simpler version of complex API the Facade handles all the dirty work and the client
remains unaware of the complex API and is only required to know the simpler version
so we build the class define the facade class to have the simpler api
implement this class using the larger more complex system